# Task 148-017: Provider Matrix — Claude + Codex Mixed Mini-Sprint

## Approach
Create a comprehensive E2E test suite that validates mixed-provider routing scenarios using mock adapters (no real API calls).

## Files to Create
1. `tests/e2e/provider-matrix/claude-codex-mixed.test.ts` — 4 test cases
2. `docs/audits/sprint-148/provider-parity.md` — Audit document

## Test Strategy
- Use `makeMockAdapter` pattern from `tests/e2e/provider-smoke.test.ts`
- Mock 3 providers: claude (available), codex (available/timeout), haiku (available)
- Test scenarios:
  1. 3-task routing: opus→claude, gpt-4.1→codex, haiku→claude
  2. Codex timeout → Claude fallback via `resolveProviderWithFallback`
  3. Per-provider metrics tracking (latency, tokens, cost simulation)
  4. Provider stats aggregation for retro format

## Key Dependencies
- `ProviderRegistry`, `resolveProviderWithFallback` from `src/core/provider.ts`
- `routeTask`, `detectTaskType` from `src/orchestra/task-router.ts`
- `getEquivalentModel`, `getModelTier` from `src/core/model-equivalence.ts`
- Mock adapter pattern from existing tests
